< A text reader that takes the largest value the trace wrote recovers more of the gap than the model's own answer (Table~\ref{tab:main}, Figure~\ref{fig:main}c), but those figures are in-sample, and on the synthetic traces it hurts four models, so it is no replacement for the answer. It works as an audit: sending decisions where reader and answer disagree to the calculator recovers 73--93\% of the gap on products not used to set its rule and 82--100\% on synthetic traces, and it beats random, low-confidence and unfinished-list triggers at the same call rate. Since calling the calculator every time recovers everything, the audit is useful only where reasoning must stay in the loop, for example to check an agent whose tools cannot be changed.
